<!-- Section: The Three Principles -->
<section class="vintage-section">
	<div class="section-head">
		<div class="section-numeral">I. The Principles</div>
		<h2 class="section-heading">Safety by Design</h2>
		<p class="section-sublead">
			Most assistants run unmonitored scripts. Sub-Sub operates under strict, code-enforced boundaries.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="principles-list">
		<div class="principle-item">
			<div class="principle-num">1.</div>
			<div class="principle-body">
				<h3>The Code-Enforced Gate</h3>
				<p>
					The model cannot modify your library on its own. Every alteration is calculated first as a dry-run preview (+added, -removed) and executed only after your explicit confirmation.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="principle-item">
			<div class="principle-num">2.</div>
			<div class="principle-body">
				<h3>Universal Journal &amp; Rollback</h3>
				<p>
					Every change is recorded in a local SQLite journal with a unique identifier. Type <code>/undo</code> at any time to restore previous metadata, tags, or items.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="principle-item">
			<div class="principle-num">3.</div>
			<div class="principle-body">
				<h3>Air-Gapped Local Privacy</h3>
				<p>
					Listens strictly on <code>127.0.0.1</code> protected by an authenticated single-origin session cookie. The Librarian operates entirely offline. Your library, notes, and citations remain on your machine.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section: The Two Offices -->
<section class="vintage-section" style="padding-top: 1rem;">
	<div class="section-head">
		<div class="section-numeral">II. The Two Offices</div>
		<h2 class="section-heading">Librarian &amp; Researcher</h2>
		<p class="section-sublead">
			Two distinct modes, each with its own tools, boundaries, and model.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="offices-wrap">
		<!-- Librarian Office -->
		<div class="office-box">
			<div class="office-head">
				<div class="office-role">The First Office</div>
				<h3>The Librarian</h3>
			</div>
			<p class="office-desc">
				Keeps your library in order. Works from controlled vocabularies and imports verified metadata.
			</p>
			<ul class="office-duties">
				<li>Tags references from your custom vocabulary in <code>Systems/Zotero tags.md</code></li>
				<li>Imports citations by DOI, PMID, or ISBN with full abstracts and citekeys</li>
				<li>Repairs metadata, flags retractions, eliminates duplicates, and fetches open-access PDFs</li>
				<li>Operates completely offline with zero unsolicited network traffic</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<!-- Researcher Office -->
		<div class="office-box">
			<div class="office-head">
				<div class="office-role">The Second Office</div>
				<h3>The Researcher</h3>
			</div>
			<p class="office-desc">
				Reads your library and surveys the wider literature without altering your collection.
			</p>
			<ul class="office-duties">
				<li>Answers "What do I have on...?" directly from your local references with citekeys</li>
				<li>Searches PubMed and OpenAlex for critical works missing from your collection</li>
				<li>Writes structured literature notes and syntheses in plain Markdown</li>
				<li>Read-only safety: cannot alter library records or delete items</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

